<<if $XavierSocial > 50>>
    Xavier Richards is the most popular boy in school thanks to the money and social status of his parents. While he can be a bit overbearing and full of himself, you still find him pretty pleasant to be around and think you’ve started to see the real boy underneath. Though whether that real boy is just a normal kind kid or a manipulative psychopath, you can’t be sure. To be fair, it might be both. <br>
    <br>
<<elseif $XavierSocial > -10>>
    Xavier Richards is the most popular boy at Preston. Coming from a family of large generational wealth, his money, social status, and generally confident and assured personality has led him to be the envy of most at your school. Still, people seem just as afraid of him as they are envious. <br>
    <br>
<<else>>
    Xavier Richards is the most popular boy at Preston, mainly due to his parents’ money and social standing. The boy is full of himself and seems to think he’s the most important person in whatever room he is in and uses his power to place himself above others. You find both his smug face and horde of followers at his beck and call to be extremely annoying. <br>
    <br>
<</if>>

<<if $CompletedQuests.includes("Xavier: Big Brother")>>
    Xavier has a little brother named Levi who is even more full of himself than Xavier is. The kid is a little twerp who even Xavier seems to find annoying. Interestingly enough, Levi seems to be just as terrified of Xavier as most of the kids in your grades. For good reasons too, as you learn that Xavier is apparently in charge of punishing the boy when he acts out. <br>
    <br>
<</if>>

